### ERROR TESTING - Testing delivery area limits

###
# @name testOutOfAreaDelivery
# Test delivery to location outside service area (should return error)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/plugins/woocommerce/clients/auth/trading-points/{{tradingPointId}}/delivery-orders/get-price HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

type=Regular
&category=Other
&real_type=ExpressDelivery
&origin[address]={{shopAddress}}
&origin[coordinates][0]={{shopCoordinatesLng}}
&origin[coordinates][1]={{shopCoordinatesLat}}
&origin[name]={{shopName}}
&origin[phone]={{shopPhone}}
&destinations[0][address]=Liepaja, Latvia
&destinations[0][coordinates][0]=21.0109
&destinations[0][coordinates][1]=56.5047
&destinations[0][name]={{customerName}}
&destinations[0][phone]={{customerPhone}}

### USING REQUEST VARIABLES - Chain requests using response data

###
# @name loginExample
# Example: If QWQER had a login endpoint (hypothetical)
# POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login HTTP/1.1
# Content-Type: {{contentType}}
# 
# username=testuser&password=testpass

###
# Example of using response from previous request
# @authToken = {{loginExample.response.headers.Authorization}}
# GET {{baseUrl}}/some-protected-endpoint HTTP/1.1
# Authorization: {{authToken}}

### ENVIRONMENT-SPECIFIC VARIABLES
### You can set these in VS Code settings:
### "rest-client.environmentVariables": {
###     "production": {
###         "token": "PRODUCTION_TOKEN",
###         "tradingPointId": "PRODUCTION_TRADING_POINT_ID"
###     },
###     "development": {
###         "token": "DEV_TOKEN",
###         "tradingPointId": "DEV_TRADING_POINT_ID"
###     }
### }